        <item>
            <title>0.2</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 15:48:14 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>484</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 484)</h2>
<p><b>A session can hold renders in different color spaces.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>The Input space now belongs to the clip.</b> Pick a space and it applies to the shot on screen and stays with it — saved in the session, so it survives version cycling and travels with the .otio. Previously the pick was stored against the FORMAT, so setting one EXR silently repainted every other EXR in the session, which made a mixed-space session impossible to set up correctly.</li>
<li><b>New: "Apply to All … Clips" in the Color pipeline popover.</b> Most sessions are mostly one space, so set it once, apply to the whole format, then deal with the outliers shot by shot. It only touches clips of the same format — applying to your EXRs leaves a slate PNG alone.</li>
<li><b>The playlist shows each clip's space</b>, so a session part-way through being set up is readable at a glance and the outliers stand out.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: a pinned space was written but then ignored.</b> The per-format default was consulted first, so setting a clip's Input appeared to do nothing. A clip's own space now beats every guess, including an optimized stand-in's record of what the encode assumed — pinning a space is precisely how you correct that.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
